          "worked": "Under this book’s convention: ambiguous. Mixed intersection and union need brackets. For $A=B=\\varnothing$ and $C=\\{1\\}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}(A\\cap B)\\cup C&=\\{1\\},\\\\A\\cap(B\\cup C)&=\\varnothing.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two groupings give different sets.",
